  "analysis": "I'm at a fresh terminal prompt. I need to:\n1. Read the run id from /logs/artifacts/run-id\n2. Create a bucket named harbor-meta-${run_id} on Tigris\n3. Upload /home/user/tigris-task/report.txt with custom metadata (owner=alice, team=research) and content-type text/markdown\n4. Verify the metadata persisted",
  "plan": "First, let me check the current state of the environment - verify the file exists, read the run id, and check the AWS configuration.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /logs/artifacts/run-id\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /home/user/tigris-task/\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /home/user/tigris-task/report.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "env | grep -i aws\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I have all the information I need:\n- Run id: zr93s41266\n- Bucket name: harbor-meta-zr93s41266 (already valid - no invalid chars)\n- File exists with content 'quarterly report' (no trailing newline - 16 bytes)\n- AWS CLI is pre-configured with the required environment variables",
  "plan": "Now I'll:\n1. Create the bucket on Tigris\n2. Upload the file with the required metadata and content-type\n3. Verify the upload",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "RUN_ID=$(cat /logs/artifacts/run-id)\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "BUCKET=\"harbor-meta-${RUN_ID}\"\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo \"Bucket name: $BUCKET\"\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "aws s3 mb s3://$BUCKET\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The bucket was created successfully. Now I need to upload the file with the required metadata and content-type.",
  "plan": "Upload the file with custom metadata (owner=alice, team=research) and content-type text/markdown, then verify with head-object.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "aws s3 cp /home/user/tigris-task/report.txt s3://$BUCKET/reports/q1.txt --metadata owner=alice,team=research --content-type text/markdown\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "File uploaded successfully. Now I need to verify the metadata persisted by running head-object.",
  "plan": "Verify the upload with head-object to confirm Content-Type is text/markdown and Metadata contains both owner=alice and team=research.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "aws s3api head-object --bucket $BUCKET --key reports/q1.txt\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The head-object command failed due to missing 'less' pager. I need to disable the pager or pipe the output to a different command.",
  "plan": "Disable the AWS CLI pager by setting AWS_PAGER to an empty string, then retry the head-object command.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "export AWS_PAGER=\"\"\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "aws s3api head-object --bucket $BUCKET --key reports/q1.txt\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

